  17:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** /** \file fsCom.c
  18:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****  *
  19:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****  *  \ingroup  <DOXY_GROUP>
  20:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****  *
  21:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****  *  \brief    Implementation of package fsCom for functional safety.
  22:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****  *
  23:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****  *  \details  <b>Functional Safety Generic Component - Top-Level Design </b>
  24:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  25:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  26:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \li <b>Package Model </b>\n
  27:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \image html Package_fscom.jpg
  28:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  29:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  30:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** The fscom package provides the parts outlined in the model. By compilation switch, the generic may 
  31:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** the usual operating mode or in test harness mode. When running in the usual operating mode, the tes
  32:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** will not be linked to the package. When running in test harness mode, a test server gets control on
  33:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** fscom.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\SX2605~1.HOD\AppData\Local\Temp\ccjsfxRg.s 			page 2


  34:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  35:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  36:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** By the test harness part, it is possible to test all functions inside fscom fully isolated from oth
  37:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** whole system. Moreover, passing parameters for certain tests and recording of the results is suppor
  38:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  39:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  40:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  41:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \li <b>State Model </b>\n
  42:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \image html StateModel_PseudoScheduler.jpg
  43:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  44:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  45:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** The pseudo-scheduler function basically schedules the task handlers for existing channels and maint
  46:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** There is one state implemented for each task. Before start of the scheduling, the system has to be 
  47:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** the initialisation state is entered by default (at completion of the startup phase).
  48:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  49:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  50:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** Some application have not implemented the scheduler component the archtecture provides. For that ra
  51:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** package aditionally has implemented a scheduling mechanism. With this scheduling mechanism, corrent
  52:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** order of channel task handler scheduling and channel checking is guaranteed.
  53:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  54:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  55:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  56:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \li <b>Scenario: Normal operational scheduling </b>\n
  57:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \image html SequenceChart_PseudoScheduler.jpg
  58:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  59:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  60:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** The generic only provides two interfaces to an application: one provide a means to setup a certain 
  61:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** be scheduled continuousely; the second interface prvide a means to schedule the generic during an a
  62:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** operational work. As said in the headline, this scenario dos not take care on some exceptions.
  63:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  64:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  65:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** The generic's execution path is split up into smaller pieces, one to be preformed on every call of 
  66:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** because service of interrupts must be performed as fast as possible. So, there is some more to do w
  67:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** interface, but ths is not an issue here. A concrete application need not make use of the generic's 
  68:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** but it has to make sure that all tests have been completed --BEFORE-- the generic gets control.
  69:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  70:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  71:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
  72:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \li<b>Input Document Reference(s) </b>\n
  73:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** \n
