1129:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****    //  Calling convention:
1130:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****    //  ALL (!) checks are called like C-functions and, on return, it has to follow the conventions
1131:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****    //  for C-functions too. But, as the stack can't be used for local variables Register and RAM
1132:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****    //  checks are called directly, not using a loop variable.
1133:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** 
