1149:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** /** End of the FSCOM boot phase.
1150:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****     At the end of the FSCOM boot phase, control is transferred directly to this routine.
1151:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****     Within this routine, start up has to continue depending on a project needs.
1152:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** 
1153:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****     \pre    FSCOM boot phase completed successfully\n
1154:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****     \post   All one-time checks have been performed successfully.
1155:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****     \note   By this routine, completion of the FSCOM process is clearly defined. For the
1156:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****             application-specific start up continuation, please refer to the interfaces
1157:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****             required by FSCOM.
1158:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** */
1159:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** /*-----------------------------------------------------------------------
1160:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****   Control Flow:
1161:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****   Begin
1162:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****       Chapter 6.5 (FSCOM Boot Procedure) requires to define one point where to continue
1163:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****       start up, from FSCOM library point of view. Hence, the boot procedure has always
1164:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****       the same point of completion and this is very helpful while debugging.
1165:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** 
1166:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****       continue the application specific system start up;
1167:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** 
1168:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****       NOTE: not return back here!
1169:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c ****   End;
1170:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** 
1171:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** 
1172:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsCom.c **** -------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
